  "yesterday_verification_summary": "Day+0 for 2026-10-08: gfs_seamless, ecmwf_ifs025, icon_seamless, ukmo_seamless and best_match called the rain right. Day+3 for 2026-10-05: ecmwf_ifs025, icon_seamless and best_match called the rain right; gfs_seamless and ukmo_seamless did not. Day+7 for 2026-10-01: ecmwf_ifs025 and best_match called the rain right; gfs_seamless did not.",
  "narrative_markdown": "## Today's Forecast\n\nShowery from the afternoon, with thunder possible from the morning, peaking this afternoon. 31°C / 87°F high, 20°C / 68°F low. Sky mostly cloudy early, partly cloudy at midday and overcast in the evening. Wind ENE early, SSW at midday and NE in the evening; gusts to 36 km/h (19 kt). UV index 9.5 (very high). Air quality 50 (good) at Kisumu Airport, the highest of 3 stations.\n\n## Extended Outlook\n\nTemperatures and winds much the same through Monday, with showers and thunderstorms likely each day. Skies mostly cloudy throughout. Monday's call: rain, 100%, with all four models wet; highs around 29 °C. At this lead ECMWF has the best record, right 77% of the time over 55 checks.\n\nFurther out, temperatures and winds much the same through Friday, with showers and thunderstorms likely Tuesday and Wednesday, and showers and thunderstorms possible Thursday and Friday. Only GFS, ECMWF and ICON reach past Wednesday. ECMWF and ICON are the wetter solutions from Tuesday to Friday; GFS and UKMO keep it drier. Friday's call: rain, 100%, with both models wet; highs 25 to 30 °C. At this lead ECMWF has the best record, right 80% of the time over 52 checks.\n\n## Winam Gulf — Conditions for Boaters\n\nPeak gust 26 km/h (14 kt). Any thunderstorm brings sudden gusts well above this figure; the water is unsafe while one is nearby.\n\nFigures issued 06:01. Written by code; a discussion follows when a model answers.\n",
